#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Train and evaluate SE-UAP according to the manuscript methodology.

Main-experiment detector setting:
    - Attacking TIMIT uses the detector pre-trained on LibriSpeech.
    - Attacking LibriSpeech uses the detector pre-trained on TIMIT.

Methodology implemented:
    z ~ N(0, I)
    delta_tilde = G_theta(z), where delta_tilde has 3200 samples (0.2 s)
    delta_base = Pi_Delta(delta_tilde), where Delta is an L2 ball with radius tau
    delta_L = repeat/truncate(delta_base, L)
    x_adv = clip(x + delta_L, -1, 1)
    L = L_rec + alpha * L_det + lambda_energy * E_raw(delta_tilde)

Here tau constrains the base universal perturbation before length adaptation.

Only the generator is updated during training. The SincNet speaker recognizer and the
pre-trained adversarial detector are frozen.

Evaluation metrics:
    FR  : fooling rate of the speaker recognizer
    FRD : detector fooling rate, i.e. adversarial audio classified as benign
    SNR : signal-to-noise ratio
    PESQ: perceptual evaluation of speech quality
    ATC : online attack time cost per sample
    SEI : FRD / ATC
"""

import argparse
import csv
